In one Continual-ARC task, two structurally different demonstrations established the same transformation: rows containing a left-aligned stripe that ended short of the right edge had only their remaining background cells changed to color 1. Rows whose stripe already reached the boundary were unchanged. The first pair used stripe/background colors 7/8; the second used 5/0, supporting color 1 as the completion color rather than a copy of the stripe. The test used a full-width row and another row stopping at column 20 of 26; thus the validated action filled just the final five cells of the partial row with 1.

